cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use mcp-daemon-diet in research or software, please cite it as below."
title: "mcp-daemon-diet"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Dziatkovskii
    given-names: Anton
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7408-3054"
    affiliation: "Palo Alto AI Research Lab"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tonydzi/mcp-daemon-diet"
url: "https://github.com/tonydzi/mcp-daemon-diet"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  One shared MCP daemon per machine instead of a stdio copy in every agent session.
  Server-agnostic and client-agnostic: the recipe, launcher and autostart templates for
  Windows, macOS and Linux (none requiring admin), a watchdog built not to make things
  worse, two measurement scripts that report copy counts and memory before and after, a
  verifier that proves both that the config is off stdio and that the daemon answers, and
  thirteen dated production failures with their fixes. Stdlib-only Python. States plainly
  what it does not do: it saves processes, sockets and locks, not tokens.
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - daemon
  - sse
  - devops
  - agent-tooling
